{"seconds": 339.6, "exit": 0, "final": "Excellent! After 2...Rxd2, Black has won the bishop (+3 material). \n\nSo the key tactical point is:\n- **1...Ne3** appears to sacrifice the knight (it's undefended)\n- But White MUST choose between Bxe3 or Rxe3\n- If **2.Bxe3**, Black plays **2...Rxe2**, winning the rook (net: Black +2)\n- If **2.Rxe3**, Black plays **2...Rxd2**, winning the bishop (net: Black 0, but favorable)\n\nIn either case, Black gets a winning advantage! The knight move **Ne3 is a fork/deflection** that forces White into a losing position.\n\nLet me verify the main line one more time:\n\n**Best move: Ne3**\n\n**Main line:** \n1...Ne3 2.Bxe3 Rxe2 (Black wins the rook, +5 material)\nor\n1...Ne3 2.Rxe3 Rxd2 (Black wins the bishop, +3 material, but rook becomes active)\n\nThe motif is: **fork** (the knight move forks the rook and bishop, forcing one to move and exposing the other) or **deflection** (the knight forces a piece to move, which exposes another piece).\n\n## Coaching Note (max 80 words):\n\n\"Look for moves where your opponent's pieces are overloaded defending each other! Your knight on e3 forks the rook and bishop\u2014both want to capture it. If the bishop takes, your rook wins the now-undefended rook. If the rook takes, your rook wins the now-undefended bishop. Either way, you win! This is a knight fork where the defenders are trapped by their own positions.\"\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Ne3\", \"line\": [\"Ne3\", \"Bxe3\", \"Rxe2\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"deflection\", \"trappedPiece\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "8/6p1/4p1k1/3pPn2/2pP4/2P3PK/1r1BR2P/8 b - - 0 51"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "8/6p1/4p1k1/3pPn2/2pP4/2P3PK/1r1BR2P/8 b - - 0 51"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "8/6p1/4p1k1/3pPn2/2pP4/2P3PK/1r1BR2P/8 b - - 0 51", "square": "e2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "8/6p1/4p1k1/3pP